  "id": "voelvry_afrikaans_rock",
  "name": "Voëlvry (1989 Afrikaans alternative rock movement)",
  "family": "rock",
  "lineage": "Afrikaans-language protest-rock movement launched by Shifty Records, whose 1989 Voëlvry tour of university campuses brought Johannes Kerkorrel en die Gereformeerde Blues Band, Koos Kombuis and Bernoldus Niemand (James Phillips) to young Afrikaner audiences. Its songs mocked apartheid and the conservative Afrikaner establishment in blues- and punk-inflected rock and are regarded as a turning point in Afrikaans popular music. The name means both 'free as a bird' and 'outlawed'.",
